; Respawn position of the player (X and Y, 8.8 fixed point)
;
; The place where the player appears when a room is entered in state 2 or 4 (#R$850C): #R$85FC copies the two words to
; the player's X and Y (#R$A8A1, #R$A8A3). The high bytes are in 2-pixel units (X 0-$7F, Y 0-$57), the low bytes are
; 0. #R$BDF3 sets the high bytes from the active checkpoint record (#R$BE2A: column*4, row*4); the passage items
; #R$A6BC and #R$A6D8 set both words to the exit of the doorway they lead to, so that after a death in the other room
; the player reappears there. The block $8512-$854D is zeroed by #R$85FC at the start of a game.
; .
; +0 word RespawnX (low byte, then RespawnXHi)
; +2 word RespawnY (low byte, then RespawnYHi)
@label=RespawnX
g$8512 DEFB $00
@label=RespawnXHi
 $8513 DEFB $00
@label=RespawnY
 $8514 DEFB $00
@label=RespawnYHi
 $8515 DEFB $00
